{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Helvetica;}}\f0\fs24 {\b Topology}\par 1. Skim - MODIFY: highlighted the credit agreement (add-back cap, 18-month window, cash netting limit, 5.25x step-down, equity cure) and the compliance certificate where it doesn't match, then exported both with notes\par 2. Google Sheets - MODIFY: marked each add-back eligible or not, applied the cap and cash netting limit, recalculated leverage and coverage, sized the cure and downloaded the workbook\par 3. Pages - CREATE: wrote the credit memo to my portfolio manager and exported it as a PDF\par \par {\b Request}\par I'm a leveraged finance associate at the agent bank on a sponsor-backed term loan, and the borrower just sent in its Q3 2026 compliance certificate. The leverage covenant steps down to 5.25x this quarter and they're reporting 5.13x, which is close enough that I want to rebuild the numbers myself instead of taking theirs at face value. I'll go through the credit agreement in Skim and mark up the EBITDA add-back cap, the cash netting limit and the equity cure section, then mark up the certificate wherever it doesn't line up with those definitions. In Google Sheets I'll check each add-back, apply the caps, recalculate leverage and interest coverage, and work out the minimum equity cure if they turn out to be out of compliance. Then I'll write a short credit memo in Pages for my portfolio manager with what I found and what I think we should do next. Deliverables are the marked-up PDFs, the covenant workbook and the memo as a PDF.\par \par {\b Task Description}\par 1. In Skim, highlight the key terms in the credit agreement: the 25% add-back cap (measured before add-backs), the 18-month cost savings window, the $15M cash netting limit, the 5.25x step-down and the equity cure.\par 2. In Skim, highlight where the borrower's certificate goes off: the cap uses EBITDA after add-backs, the Dayton savings land too late, and all $28M of cash was netted.\par 3. In Google Sheets, mark each add-back eligible or not and apply the 25% cap and the cash netting limit.\par 4. In Google Sheets, check the recalculated leverage and interest coverage against the covenant, size the minimum cure and download the workbook.\par 5. In Pages, write a short credit memo with the result, the findings and my recommendation, and export it as a PDF.\par }